steps:
- args: [share]
  exit_code: 0
  stdout: "Do you want to share your own Step with the world? Awesome!\n\nJust follow
    these steps:\n\n0. First, you need to ensure that your step is stored in a public
    git repository\nand it follows our step development guideline: https://github.com/bitrise-io/bitrise/blob/master/_docs/step-development-guideline.md.\n\nTo
    audit your step on your local machine call $ stepman audit --step-yml path/to/your/step.yml\n\n1.
    Fork the StepLib repository you want to share your Step in.\nYou can find the
    main (\"official\") StepLib repository at https://github.com/bitrise-io/bitrise-steplib\n\n2.
    Call $ stepman share start -c https://github.com/[your-username]/bitrise-steplib.git,
    with the git clone URL of your forked StepLib repository.\nThis will prepare your
    forked StepLib locally for sharing.\n\n3. Next, call $ stepman share create --tag
    [step-version-tag] --git [step-git-uri].git --stepid [step-id],\nto add your Step
    to your forked StepLib repository (locally).\n\nImportant: you have to add the
    (version) tag to your Step's repository.\n\n4. You can call $ stepman audit -c
    https://github.com/[your-username]/bitrise-steplib.git \nto perform a complete
    health-check on your forked StepLib before submitting your Pull Request.\n\nThis
    can help you catch issues which might prevent your Step from being accepted.\n\n5.
    Almost done! You should review your Step's step.yml file (the one added to the
    local StepLib),\nand once you're happy with it call $ stepman share finish\n\nThis
    will commit & push the step.yml into your forked StepLib repository.\n\n6. The
    only remaining thing is to create a Pull Request in the original StepLib repository.
    And you are done!\n\n"
- args: [share, start, -c, 'file://$STEPLIB']
  exit_code: 0
  stdout: |+
    Validating Step share params...
    all inputs are valid

    Preparing StepLib...
    StepLib prepared at: $WORK/home/.stepman/step_collections/$ALIAS/collection

    Next, call $ stepman share create --tag [step-version-tag] --git [step-git-uri].git --stepid [step-id],
    to add your Step to your forked StepLib repository (locally).

    Important: you have to add the (version) tag to your Step's repository.

  changed_files:
    home/.stepman/routing.json: "{\n\t\"file://$STEPLIB\": \"$ALIAS\"\n}"
    home/.stepman/share.json: "{\n\t\"Collection\": \"file://$STEPLIB\",\n\t\"StepID\":
      \"\",\n\t\"StepTag\": \"\"\n}"
    home/.stepman/step_collections/$ALIAS/collection/LICENSE: |
      MIT License

      Copyright (c) 2024 Bitrise

      Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
      of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal
      in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights
      to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
      copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is
      furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:

      The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all
      copies or substantial portions of the Software.

      THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.
    home/.stepman/step_collections/$ALIAS/collection/README.md: |
      # Stepman integration-test fixture steplib

      A minimal steplib layout consumed by the golden parity suite in
      `_tests/integration`. The runner copies this tree into a temp dir,
      turns it into a git repo, and points `stepman` subcommands at it over
      `file://`. Not used by any live step or by the public steplib index.

      Contents:

      - `steplib.yml` — minimal collection metadata.
      - `steps/test-step/1.0.0/step.yml` — one well-formed step version.
    home/.stepman/step_collections/$ALIAS/collection/steplib.yml: |
      format_version: 1.0.0
      steplib_source: https://github.com/bitrise-io/stepman-fixture-steplib.git
      assets_download_base_uri: ""
      download_locations:
      - type: git
        src: source/git
    home/.stepman/step_collections/$ALIAS/collection/steps/test-step/1.0.0/step.yml: <1091
      bytes, sha256 c45c472ce64eb9a74bea2a94f449bbe132c9b48f33a746034b96dd1a9c7436d1>
    home/.stepman/step_collections/$ALIAS/spec/slim-spec.json: <2327 bytes, sha256
      cce1032e2be7e53b35b0ee7fa9441ed5c81de73427fef3102122f493804c85b2>
    home/.stepman/step_collections/$ALIAS/spec/spec.json: <2327 bytes, sha256 cce1032e2be7e53b35b0ee7fa9441ed5c81de73427fef3102122f493804c85b2>
